    "title": "Texas, Oklahoma, Arkansas, Tennessee, Kentucky, Virginia, North Carolina and New Jersey Brace for Long-Duration Winter Storm With Heavy Snow, Ice and Dangerous Cold - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nina Clarke ,\n17 hours ago UNITED STATES — A long-duration and increasingly high-impact winter storm is taking shape across a wide swath of the central and eastern United States, with forecast guidance now showing a prolonged period of heavy snow, significant ice accumulation, and dangerous cold stretching from the Texas Panhandle through the Mid-South, Appalachians, and into the Mid-Atlantic and Northeast between Friday, January 23 and Monday, January 26. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 27",
